here we will learn about the classes and the inharitance 

let's explain class step by step with example
step 1 creating a class
class chai():
    origin = "india" we created class by calling through name called chai()
    this  origin is created inside the class is called class attributes 
    it belongs to class itelf.

step 2  will be accessing class atributes 
print(chai.origin) output will be india because it belongs to the class


step 3 adding another class attribute dynamically
chai.is_hot =True 
now this attribute also become the part of this class 
chai
 ├── origin = "india"
 └── is_hot = True

step 4 creating object
masala = chai()
Now masala is an object (instance) of class chai.

step 5 accesssing attributes through object 
print(f"masala{masala.origin}"
output masala india )

same thing happens with here print(f"masala {masala.is_hot}")
masala True
because object borrows the class attribute


step 6 overriding attribute in object

 masla.chai.is_hot = False
 IMPORTANT PART 🚨

Now Python creates a NEW attribute inside the object.

Now memory looks like:

chai
 ├── origin = "india"
 └── is_hot = True

masala
 └── is_hot = False

 IMPORTANT note masala is an instance of chai